clearhead-core/crates/clearhead-core/src/workspace/transaction.rs:573: should-fix: 4#4 Occurrence resolution keeps a second, separately loaded copy of the workspace (occurrence_transaction_input) in sync with the transaction model by copying every action across after each operation, then copies the charter's actions back by matching a built 'charters/<file>' path string. Source-file writes from the occurrence batch are then filtered out. — Two in-memory copies of the same files are reconciled by hand on every operation, and an inconsistency check papers over the gap. The runbook says this kind of second read must be fixed or escalated as NEEDS DECISION, not shipped. The fold should work on a single model.
